1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,902
A: Most pharmacies still run on fax machines, phone calls, paper logs, and systems that don't talk to each other.

2
00:00:05,902 --> 00:00:09,630
A: The lot, the patient, and the prescription live in three different places.

3
00:00:09,690 --> 00:00:17,137
A: Chimera Rx shows what a modern pharmacy looks like: one connected ledger, from the dock to the pickup counter, with every step on the record.

4
00:00:17,197 --> 00:00:19,190
B: We stay in the pharmacist's view.

5
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:26,500
B: Today shows their own work: deliveries to check in, stock to watch, and suggestions from the AI agents, all in one place.

6
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,178
B: Receiving starts at the dock.

7
00:00:28,178 --> 00:00:34,972
B: One scan with the camera reads the lot, serial, and expiry from the label, with no typing and no paper log.

8
00:00:35,032 --> 00:00:39,348
B: Four checks run: the invoice, the paperwork, the expiry, and the recall list.

9
00:00:39,348 --> 00:00:42,004
B: The lot is captured, and put-away is recorded.

10
00:00:42,064 --> 00:00:45,810
B: At the counter, Rx Guardian reviews an order the moment it arrives.

11
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:51,429
B: It shows what it found, and the evidence from the patient's own history, so nothing is a guess.

12
00:00:51,489 --> 00:00:57,269
B: Accept the suggestion, and the order goes on hold with the reason recorded in the audit log.

13
00:00:57,269 --> 00:00:58,629
B: The pharmacist always decides.

14
00:00:58,689 --> 00:00:59,927
A: Now the AI agents.

15
00:00:59,927 --> 00:01:08,281
A: Eight of them work in the background, and every one follows one rule: rules decide, the model explains, a gate checks the model, and a pharmacist decides.

16
00:01:08,341 --> 00:01:11,906
B: Rx Guardian works on its own, even when nobody is looking.

17
00:01:11,906 --> 00:01:15,795
B: Run it now, and it flags what a busy pharmacist could miss.

18
00:01:15,795 --> 00:01:17,739
B: It never changes an order itself.

19
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:22,303
B: Pick any provider: Bedrock, Anthropic, an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a local model.

20
00:01:22,303 --> 00:01:27,934
B: Patient names and birth dates stay out of the prompts, and every run is logged.

21
00:01:27,994 --> 00:01:29,885
A: Here is the gap old systems leave.

22
00:01:29,885 --> 00:01:36,100
A: When a recall arrives, nobody knows which patients got which lot, so you either warn everyone, or you warn no one at all.

23
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:38,245
B: Connected, one lookup finds the recall.

24
00:01:38,245 --> 00:01:43,457
B: The pharmacist confirms each lot, and the screen shows the units and the patients affected.

25
00:01:43,517 --> 00:01:47,456
B: Messages are drafted for exactly those patients, and no one else.

26
00:01:47,456 --> 00:01:51,753
B: The pharmacist attests, and only then do they reach the sandbox outbox.

27
00:01:51,813 --> 00:01:53,123
A: Everything speaks open standards.

28
00:01:53,123 --> 00:02:02,618
A: Partners connect through a REST API, an MCP server, FHIR behind OAuth, and signed webhooks, and every call is checked against its scopes and written to the audit log.

29
00:02:02,678 --> 00:02:14,161
A: The real-world connections, like text, email, phone, wholesaler, e-prescribing, the health record, payer, and single sign-on, are designed seams, sandboxed today, so nothing reaches a real person while you evaluate it.

30
00:02:14,221 --> 00:02:16,537
A: Roles are enforced on the server.

31
00:02:16,537 --> 00:02:21,168
A: A cashier only sees pickup and the register, never allergies or recalls.

32
00:02:21,168 --> 00:02:24,256
A: An admin only manages partner access, nothing clinical.

33
00:02:24,316 --> 00:02:25,844
A: Security is built in.

34
00:02:25,844 --> 00:02:31,573
A: PHI fields are encrypted, and the audit log is hash-chained, so any tampering shows up.

35
00:02:31,573 --> 00:02:33,865
A: These are HIPAA-style safeguards, not certified.

36
00:02:33,925 --> 00:02:34,819
A: Built with Kiro.

37
00:02:34,819 --> 00:02:39,888
A: Specs carry requirement IDs, steering holds the safety rules, and hooks run a PHI guard on save.

38
00:02:39,888 --> 00:02:44,957
A: A custom agent and a Kiro Crew team did the work, with a human at every gate.

39
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:45,952
A: Chimera Rx.

40
00:02:45,952 --> 00:02:47,823
A: github.com/pjborad/Chimera-Rx.

41
00:02:47,823 --> 00:02:49,694
A: pjborad.github.io/Chimera-Rx.

